### =====================================================================
### Flat Meal Manager: manual API tests
### Needs the VS Code extension "REST Client" (by Huachao Mao).
### Click "Send Request" above each request, from top to bottom.
### The backend must be running (mvn spring-boot:run).
### =====================================================================

@base = http://localhost:8080/api


### 1. Health check (no login needed)
GET {{base}}/health


### 2. Log in as the first manager (created automatically on first start)
# @name managerLogin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "manager",
  "password": "changeme123"
}

@managerToken = {{managerLogin.response.body.token}}


### 3. Who am I?
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}


### 4. Change the manager password (do this once, then use the new one in step 2)
# POST {{base}}/auth/change-password
# Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# {
#   "currentPassword": "changeme123",
#   "newPassword": "a-much-better-password"
# }


### 5. Rename the manager's member record to your real name (member 1)
PUT {{base}}/members/1
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Anila"
}


### 6. Add a member
# @name addSrijila
POST {{base}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Srijila",
  "joinedOn": "2026-10-01"
}

@srijilaId = {{addSrijila.response.body.id}}


### 7. Adding the same name again → 409 Conflict
POST {{base}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "srijila"
}


### 8. Blank name → 400 with a field error
POST {{base}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   "
}


### 9. List all members
GET {{base}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}


### 10. Create a login for Srijila
POST {{base}}/members/{{srijilaId}}/login
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "srijila",
  "password": "srijila-pass-123"
}


### 11. Log in as Srijila (a normal member)
# @name memberLogin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "srijila",
  "password": "srijila-pass-123"
}

@memberToken = {{memberLogin.response.body.token}}


### 12. Members CAN see the member list → 200
GET {{base}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}


### 13. Members CANNOT add members → 403 Forbidden
POST {{base}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sneaky"
}


### 14. Members CANNOT deactivate anyone → 403 Forbidden
POST {{base}}/members/1/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}


### 15. No token at all → 401 Unauthorized
GET {{base}}/members


### 16. Wrong password → 401 with a message
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "srijila",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}


### 17. Manager deactivates Srijila (history is kept)
POST {{base}}/members/{{srijilaId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "leftOn": "2026-10-11"
}


### 18. Only active members
GET {{base}}/members?status=ACTIVE
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}


### 19. Bring Srijila back
POST {{base}}/members/{{srijilaId}}/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
